TIP:  The song builds through the first verse and chorus.  The opening verse begins with a sweeping strum of (C) and light strums for the rest of the verse.  The first chorus is a bit stronger but still somewhat subdued.  Start the second verse with a nice bass sweep of (C) and punch it up.

TIP:  I like to include the Barcelona opening.  To do so in this key untransposed, first form (C) but lift off the middle finger.  Now pick open 4th string <d>, open 3rd string <g>, middle finger down on 3rd string/3rd fret <a>, lift off an pick open 3rd string <g>.      


